--- currentuser\software\gxwi-event-viewer
canonical: CurrentUser\Software\gxwi-event-viewer

Personal saved metric dashboards.

Event Viewer reads these settings as the session account. Access follows
the key's registry security. Saving dashboards needs write access.

--- currentuser\software\gxwi-event-viewer dashboards
canonical: CurrentUser\Software\gxwi-event-viewer Dashboards
type: REG_MULTI_SZ
default: (absent: built-in health dashboard)
valid: dashboard and chart lines as described below
applies: restart (when Event Viewer opens)

Ordered dashboards and their metric charts.

Each string starts a dashboard or adds a chart to the preceding dashboard.
The format is `dashboard SPAN NAME` or
`chart METRIC TRANSFORM FUNCTION GROUPING`, with spaces between fields.
A name can contain spaces and must contain non-whitespace text.

SPAN is `15m`, `1h`, `6h`, `24h`, or `7d`. TRANSFORM is `none`, `rate`,
`delta`, `p50`, `p95`, or `p99`. FUNCTION is `avg`, `min`, `max`, or `sum`.
GROUPING is `one` for a combined series or `each` for separate series.
METRIC names a metric known to eventd; the query service checks its meaning.

The reader accepts at most 64 dashboards and 32 charts per dashboard.
Malformed lines are skipped. A chart needs a preceding accepted dashboard.
An absent value or a list with no accepted dashboard selects the built-in
health dashboard. Read errors or a wrong registry type also select that
dashboard and display an explanation. Reading does not repair the value.

The viewer's own dashboard controls update the open window and save this
value. Reopen the viewer to load changes made by another program.
